From 65f958fea5dff229f8f69df681f3868f4f3704f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sukrit Jaidee <45908411+SukritJaAIproject@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:04:21 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): show the running edition and its bundled
 benchmark

Two editions of the desktop app (the current line and the 2026-09-12
snapshot) were indistinguishable on screen: the Overview leaderboard was
hard-coded research constants, no version or model id was shown, and
both windows were titled "iMPS".

- Sidecar /health now reports productName, appVersion (passed by the
  Electron launcher as --product-name / --app-version), artifactVersion
  and modelCreatedAt from models/manifest.json, and summarySnapshotAt.
- Dashboard hero shows edition chips (product + version, model artifact,
  benchmark data date) in desktop mode; api.ts gains
  isDesktopFaultDetectionApi(), parseDesktopRuntimeStatus(),
  getDesktopRuntimeStatus() (identity fields optional for old sidecars).
- Overview opens with "Benchmark shipped with this edition" read from the
  bundled data/summary.json (dataset counts, ranked 5-model leaderboard,
  scoring basis stated); the fixed research panel is labelled as identical
  in every edition. Web deployments get service wording instead.
- The BrowserWindow keeps the product name as its title (page-title-updated
  is suppressed) so two installed editions differ in the taskbar.
- Version 1.2.1; README documents the header and the 1.1.1 snapshot recipe
  (current dashboard + frozen 1.1.0 models/data).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
